customer: young_entrepreneur
problem: gpu_overheating
brief:
	The deletion event. A Win95 [x] floats over him all of day 6, also when he picks up, and only that day: the one exception to the [x] being for regular customers only. A click deletes him: he and his computer vanish (also from the counter) and are never mentioned again, except at the end. His voice glitches with Cambion.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello. Do you do business computers?
+ What's your business?
	(happy) Import and export. Mostly import. Okay, mostly ideas, so far.
+ So, what's your problem?
	(problem) My computer won't start. It just shows a bunch of text, something about a disk.
	+ Did you put a floppy in?
		(thinking) Just some software a guy gave me. Business stuff. Very cutting edge.
	- OK, leave it with me. [end]
		(neutral) Great. Time is money, you know.
